<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15333" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ēgressĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		egredior, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a going out</i> or <i>forth</i>
			(post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nocturna (ex castello),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 8, p. 208, 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 78, 1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eorum ex Aegypto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Num. 1, 1</span></i>
			; and so in gen. of <i>the Exodus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">filiorum Israel,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 33, 38</span></i>
			; 1 Reg. 18, 30.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, in rhet. lang., <i>a
				digression</i> in speaking, like <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρέκβασις</span>, <i><span class="en">Quint. 4,
				3, 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">15</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">3, 9, 4</span></i>; cf.
				<i><span class="en">ib. 4,
			3</span></i>: de egressione.—In plur., <i><span class="en">id. 11,
				3, 164</span></i>; <i><span class="en">12,
				10, 60</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
